      "evidence": "Step 2.1 reads: \"For $n$ even, a differential $d_r:E_r^{p,q}\\to E_r^{p+r,q-r+1}$ with source in an even coefficient row has odd target coefficient row $q-r+1$ when $r$ is odd, and zero target column when $r$ is even\". With $q$ even and the page supported in the columns $p\\in\\{0,n\\}$ ($n$ even), the two cases are exchanged: for $r$ odd, $q-r+1$ is even, and the target vanishes because the target column $p+r$ is odd (hence not $0$ or $n$); for $r$ even the target column can be $n$ (e.g. $p=0$, $r=n$), and the target vanishes because the row $q-n+1$ is odd. The sibling item `ex-complex-k-ahss-for-a-closed-oriented-surface`, step 2.1, states the correct pairing (\"target in the odd coefficient row $q-r+1$ when $r$ is even, and in the column $p+r>2$ when $r$ is odd\"). The conclusion \"in either case the target vanishes\" is true, so only the case analysis is defective.",
