      "evidence": "The Example sets \"$x:=c_1(\\gamma^*)$\" and [F1] records $c_1(L^*)=-c_1(L)$, so $c_1(\\gamma)=-x$. [F5] then states \"$H^*(\\mathbb{CP}^n;\\mathbb Z)=\\mathbb Z[x]/(x^{n+1})$ with $x=e(\\gamma_{\\mathbb R})$ the class of the tautological line\", while `def-chern-classes-from-the-projective-bundle-relation` states for a complex line that $c_1(L)=e(L_{\\mathbb R})$; hence $e(\\gamma_{\\mathbb R})=c_1(\\gamma)=-x$, so [F5] identifies the item's $x$ with $-x$, i.e. asserts $2x=0$ in $H^2(\\mathbb{CP}^n;\\mathbb Z)$. That is false: the item's own step 2.1 computes $x|_{\\mathbb{CP}^1}=-c_1(\\gamma|_{\\mathbb{CP}^1})\\neq0$ and concludes that $x$ generates an infinite cyclic group (the cited lemma `lem-integral-cohomology-ring-of-complex-projective-space-by-splitting` defines its generator as $x=e(\\gamma_{\\mathbb R})=c_1(\\gamma)$, the negative of the item's $x$). No step of the verification uses the false clause (step 2.1 uses only the restriction isomorphism and the nonzero restriction), so the defect is confined to [F5], where the letter $x$ denotes two opposite classes.",
      "severity": "nonfatal",
      "observed_sha256": "b40b3d8893df3f3cbdc2da9d37d30d663ffb0b2e804c21c742f62455dd4d2b2f"
    },
