      "evidence": "The source note claims: \"The standing normalization of this pair is that $u$ of the published projective ring is $c_1(\\gamma^*)$ for the dual tautological line, equivalently $j_b^*x=-u$\". The item's own [F7] states $H^*(\\mathbb{CP}^\\infty;\\mathbb Z)=\\mathbb Z[u]$ with $u=e(\\gamma_{\\mathbb R})$, citing `lem-cohomology-ring-of-infinite-complex-projective-space`, whose statement defines \"$u=e(\\gamma_{\\mathbb R})\\in H^2(\\mathbb{CP}^\\infty;\\mathbb Z)$\" as the class of the tautological complex line. By `def-chern-classes-from-the-projective-bundle-relation` ($c_1(L)=e(L_{\\mathbb R})$) and `prop-first-chern-class-of-tensor-dual-and-conjugate-lines` ($c_1(L^*)=-c_1(L)$), $e(\\gamma_{\\mathbb R})=c_1(\\gamma)=-c_1(\\gamma^*)$: the published generator is $-c_1(\\gamma^*)$, not $c_1(\\gamma^*)$; and for the published $u$ the item's steps 2.1-2.2 give $j_b^*x=e((j_b^*\\gamma_E)_{\\mathbb R})=+u$, not $-u$. The claim is in a source note and the item's mathematical content (a global sign, never used in steps 4.1-5.1) is unaffected.",
