      "evidence": "The page writes \"... with the dual class the generator normalized by the pair; ... Over $S^2$ the clutching degree computes the first Chern number, $c_1(E_d)=d\\,u$ for the Hopf-normalized generator $u$, ...\". The dual class is $c_1(\\gamma^*)$ and, by `ex-chern-class-of-tautological-and-hyperplane-lines-on-complex-projective-space` (\"With the pair's normalization, $x$ is the positive generator ... and $c_1(\\gamma)$ is the negative generator\", $x=c_1(\\gamma^*)$), the pair's normalized generator is $c_1(\\gamma^*)$. The item summarised by the second sentence, `ex-complex-line-bundles-over-the-two-sphere-by-clutching-degree`, sets $u:=c_1(E_1)$ with $E_1$ the line clutched by $z\\mapsto z$, which the published `def-clutching-construction-for-bundles-over-a-suspension` identifies with the tautological Hopf line $\\gamma$ (\"$g(z)=z$ gives the chosen tautological Hopf line over $S^2=\\mathbb{CP}^1$\"); hence $u=c_1(\\gamma)=-c_1(\\gamma^*)=-x$. So the page labels two opposite generators by normalization language and does not record that the two normalizations use opposite orientations of $S^2=\\mathbb{CP}^1$; each item is internally consistent (the clutching item defines its orientation by $\\langle u,[S^2]\\rangle=+1$), so the defect is the page prose, not an item claim. This independently confirms reader finding `reader:9:1`.",
