      "evidence": "[F2] states that the differential \"is the composite $k\\circ j$ of the exact-couple structure maps in the indexing of the generation theorem\", and step 1.1 repeats \"The differential is $d_1=k\\circ j$ in the exact-couple indexing\". In the cited conventions $j:D\\to E$ is the connecting map and $k:E\\to D$ the pair map (`def-exact-couple`), and the library writes the initial differential as $d=jk$ (`def-derived-exact-couple`: \"let $d=jk$\"; `thm-an-exact-couple-generates-a-spectral-sequence`, step 2.1: \"At $r=1$ this rule is the original $jk$\"). A class of $E_1^{p,q}$ is first sent by $k$ to $h^{p+q}(X^p)$ and then by $j$ to $h^{p+q+1}(X^{p+1},X^p)$, i.e. by $j\\circ k=jk$; the written $k\\circ j$ is the composite $D\\to E\\to D$, a map on $D$, not a map from $E$ to $E$. The item's own prose gives the correct order and the cellular-coboundary identification is unaffected, so the defect is the reversed, ill-typed composite symbol.",
